Stdin is read one byte at a time from the fd rather than slurped, so like [38;5;10mscanf[0m the program answers as soon as both fields are available. Confirmed with a pipe held open by [38;5;10msleep 5[0m: both binaries print and exit immediately instead of blocking for EOF.[0m[0m
